		{"id":"6a8a0a5b65ad3fb0","type":"text","text":"Woodwoses hold no long-lasting grudges. Their emotions are strong, but short-lived. They spend most of their time having fun. They age and die like any other race, but don't care about the shortness of their lives.\nDespite their primitive lifestyle, they are the inventors of musical instruments as well as the first bows. Their archers are capable of shooting arrows made of raw emotion -- sort of a proto-psychic power.\nTheir speaking style is as simple as can be, though not braindead or 'unga bunga' as it were. ","x":-1137,"y":540,"width":540,"height":280}
